  "notes": "Title: 'TIL 113 Photo darlington coupler'. One outer box holds an LED (diode triangle pointing down with bar; anode pin 1 at top, cathode pin 2 at bottom) and two transistors in darlington form: both collectors joined (dot) to pin 5 at top, first emitter (arrow) drives the second base, second emitter (arrow) to pin 4 at bottom, first base line bent down to pin 6 at bottom. All drawn as marks. No signal names printed."
